import Mathlib

namespace Erdos390

/-
# Erdős Problem 390

Let $f(n)$ be the minimal $m$ such that $n! = a_1\cdots a_k$ with $n < a_1 < \cdots < a_k = m$.
Is there (and what is it) a constant $c$ such that
$$f(n) - 2n \sim c\frac{n}{\log n}?$$

Erdős, Guy and Selfridge showed $f(n) - 2n \asymp n/\log n$; the question of the finer
asymptotic with a constant is what `erdos_390` answers, affirmatively.

`formalF` is a literal copy of the extremal function used by `formal-conjectures`, and
`formalF_rhs` supplies the constant explicitly, so `erdos_390` is exactly the right-hand side
of that repository's `erdos_390` statement.

Vendored from `ShouqiaoW/erdos` (`390/lean`, the closure of
`Erdos390.WholePaper.FormalConjecturesBridge`) together with the closure of
`PrimeNumberTheoremAnd.MediumPNT` at the revision that repository pins. The upstream
`Erdos390.*` namespaces are merged into this file's single `Erdos390` namespace.

Note that erdosproblems.com still lists this problem as open. Proof claim 88 there, by
Shouqiao Wang, gives the constant explicitly as `4029639598 / 25970038185` and links a
manuscript (`390/paper.pdf` in the same repository); the site has not accepted the claim,
and the development below is machine-checked but not reviewed by a human reader.
-/

